# `corners[corners.length - 1 - i]`: the list read from its end. The list is only guessed in front of the loop, so in the preview its length is anything; the look ahead notes the length of what is proven or
# guessed to be a list as a whole number, follows whole numbers through + - * and %, and takes that note for the key of a read. So the list is among those tested in front, the turn is quiet, the variables
# of the file are read in front of the loop, and the helper is copied into it (frame 1). No rule reads the shape of the key: `(i + 1) % corners.length` goes the same way.
